WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.700
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.800
I chose librarianship because I like 
being introduced to new ideas, and new

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:15.800
knowledge on a constant basis, and I 
found that I also like learning new

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.200
technology and I found librarianship to 
be sort of a good fit for this.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.200
I'm very interested in library automation...

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.400
A general interest in technology.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:30.000
And as I was studying library science, 
I was gravitating towards the areas of

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.300
working with automated processing of data 
and software solutions to library problems.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.600
I was very interested in the field of 
medical informatics and the role that

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:49.700
librarians could possibly play, and I 
couldn't have found a more exciting place.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.700
The role of the library is changing. So 
again, I think it's a very exciting time

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.900
to be in libraries, because we don't have...
We have the traditional role, but it's

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.400
expanded so much, because with the Internet 
and all of that, we have so many other

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.100
services that the library provides.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:11.100
Libraries offer me the opportunity to 
provide services to people, and also

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.500
I'm always interested in 
computer technologies.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.600
My job combines services and 
computer technology.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.300
I've been both in academia and private 
sector before, and then with this...

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:29.900
with NLM, I think when it's anything 
to do with biomedical information,

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.500
this is the place to be with its...you know, 
a hundred and seventy-five year tradition of

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.800
making biomedical information accessible.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:42.200
It's great to work at NLM. I think I will 
retire from here.

